SKILL: showboat (.claude/skills/showboat/SKILL.md) — read it before asking, so the ask is accurate.

Ask for a demo file under demos/ that interleaves narrative, real ./forgejo-mcp --cli invocations, and genuinely captured output. Point at demos/README.md for the house shape and the nearest existing demo as a template.

Make the ask actionable, not bureaucratic:
  - name the tool (uvx showboat; init/note/exec/pop) and say showboat exec captures output so nothing is hand-written;
  - propose a concrete path (one new demos/<topic>.md is usually less churn than editing three) plus the demos/README.md index line;
  - require ${FORGEJO_MCP_BIN:-forgejo-mcp} over absolute paths;
  - enumerate what to show by mapping it onto the scenarios in THEIR OWN spec delta;
  - state the one hard rule: captured output only.

Be honest about enforcement: check-spec-demo-anchors.sh only gates specs that opt in with '<!-- demos-anchored: true -->'. If this change has not opted in, the demo is convention, not a gate — phrase it as a request and tell the human it is not a blocker.

ALWAYS close with a real offer to record the demo yourself and push it to their branch. Do not let paperwork sink a good feature.

DONE: comment posted with the offer explicit.

A PR surfaces work that is not the PR's job (thin test coverage, absent docs, adjacent dead code). File it; do not smuggle it into the contributor's diff.

AGENT: spawn a background general-purpose agent — this is fan-out reading across a package and you want the conclusion, not the file dumps. Brief it to:
  1. run 'bd prime' first for the repo's workflow;
  2. measure the real gap ('go test -cover' on the relevant packages), not a vibe;
  3. CHECK FOR DUPLICATES with bd list / bd ready before creating anything;
  4. create ONE bead enumerating specific handlers and untested paths;
  5. commit and push nothing, modify no source.

Demand it distinguish what is on main from what only exists in the PR branch — a bead describing code that has not merged yet is a trap for the next reader. (On #481 the agent correctly caught that file_path was not on main and scoped the bead accordingly.)

DONE: bead id(s) reported, no duplicates created.
